Relevant tables / columns and their potential usage  
• PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS  
  – "publication_number": key for joining with other tables.  
  – "filing_date": numeric YYYYMMDD → extract filing year of each patent.  
  – "application_number", "title_localized", "ipc": optional context.  

• PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB  
  – "publication_number": key for joining.  
  – "embedding_v1": vector that can be used to compute cosine / dot‑product similarity.  
  – "similar": pre‑computed list (VARIANT) of the most‑similar patents with their scores; use to avoid on‑the‑fly vector math.  
  – "abstract", "title": optional context.  

Conditions that may be useful  
1. Target patent: "US-9741766-B2".  
2. Filing year must match the filing year of the target patent.  
3. Technological similarity captured by the similarity score stored inside "similar".  
4. Order descending by similarity score and keep the first five records.  


Ten exploratory → final Snowflake SQL queries  
(All column names wrapped in double quotes; LIMIT 20 for inspection.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Inspect basic bibliographic info for the target patent in PUBLICATIONS
SELECT 
    "publication_number",
    "filing_date",
    "grant_date",
    "title_localized"
FROM 
    PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE 
    "publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Derive the filing year of the target patent
SELECT 
    "publication_number",
    LEFT(TO_VARCHAR("filing_date"),4) AS "filing_year"
FROM 
    PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE 
    "publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Retrieve the embedding & similar‑patent list for the target patent
SELECT 
    "publication_number",
    "embedding_v1",
    "similar"
FROM 
    PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB
WHERE 
    "publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Flatten the "similar" array to view raw elements (publication numbers & scores)
SELECT  
    f.value AS "similar_entry"
FROM 
    PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB t,
    LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."similar") f
WHERE 
    t."publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Extract publication number & similarity score for each similar patent
SELECT  
    f.value:"publication_number"::STRING   AS "similar_pub",
    f.value:"score"::FLOAT                 AS "similarity_score"
FROM 
    PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB t,
    LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."similar") f
WHERE 
    t."publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
ORDER BY 
    "similarity_score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Join similar patents with PUBLICATIONS to fetch their filing dates
SELECT  
    s."similar_pub",
    p."filing_date"
FROM (
    SELECT  
        f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "similar_pub",
        f.value:"score"::FLOAT               AS "similarity_score"
    FROM 
        PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB t,
        LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."similar") f
    WHERE 
        t."publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
) s
LEFT JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS p
ON  s."similar_pub" = p."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Keep only those similar patents filed in the same year as the target patent
WITH target AS (
    SELECT LEFT(TO_VARCHAR("filing_date"),4) AS "target_year"
    FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
    WHERE "publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
)
SELECT  
    s."similar_pub",
    s."similarity_score",
    LEFT(TO_VARCHAR(p."filing_date"),4) AS "filing_year"
FROM (
    SELECT  
        f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "similar_pub",
        f.value:"score"::FLOAT               AS "similarity_score"
    FROM 
        PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB t,
        LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."similar") f
    WHERE 
        t."publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
) s
JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS p
    ON s."similar_pub" = p."publication_number"
JOIN target
    ON LEFT(TO_VARCHAR(p."filing_date"),4) = target."target_year"
ORDER BY 
    s."similarity_score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Count how many similar patents share the filing year with the target
WITH target_year AS (
    SELECT LEFT(TO_VARCHAR("filing_date"),4) AS "yr"
    FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
    WHERE "publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
)
SELECT 
    COUNT(*) AS "same_year_similar_count"
FROM (
    SELECT  
        f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "similar_pub"
    FROM 
        PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB t,
        LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."similar") f
    WHERE 
        t."publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
) s
JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS p
  ON s."similar_pub" = p."publication_number"
JOIN target_year ty
  ON LEFT(TO_VARCHAR(p."filing_date"),4) = ty."yr"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Ensure we have distinct similar publication numbers before ranking
WITH ranked AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT 
        f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "similar_pub",
        f.value:"score"::FLOAT               AS "similarity_score"
    FROM 
        PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB t,
        LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."similar") f
    WHERE 
        t."publication_number" = 'US-9741766-B2'
)
SELECT *
FROM ranked
ORDER BY "similarity_score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
